    "a": 0,
    "r": "Chronic environmental arsenic exposure (via groundwater or industrial dust) is a known human carcinogen, causing skin, lung, and bladder cancers, along with characteristic skin changes (hyperkeratosis of palms/soles and 'raindrop' pigmentation)."
